      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخنّث</span></b>  <i>It</i> (a thing, S) <i>bent,</i> or <i>became bent.</i>
(S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَنِثَ</span>, q. v. (A, * L, K.)
And <i>He</i> (a man) <i>acted in the manner of the</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخِنَّث</span> [or <i>effeminate,</i> &amp;c.]. (TA.) [<i>He became
a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَنَّث</span>: used in this sense in the S and K in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طوس</span>.] And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخنّث فِى كَلَامِهِ</span> [<i>He was
soft,</i> or <i>effeminate, in his speech</i>]. (S, Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
<i>He</i> (a man &amp;c.) <i>fell down by reason of weakness.</i>
(TA.)

